# Coati Scavenger: the "if there are four or more permanent cards in your graveyard" (CR 603.4, 110.4a) counts Bot1's graveyard only.
# Bot1 has three there when Coati enters: two Plains milled by Thought Scour and Black Lotus, sacrificed for mana as Coati is cast
# (Thought Scour is no permanent card). Bot2's Ornithopter, discarded to hand size, makes four permanent cards in the two graveyards,
# which do not count: the trigger never goes on the stack (with a target to choose it would have stopped for one), so nothing
# returns. (The scenarios with exactly four are the positive controls.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Thought Scour
Black Lotus
Coati Scavenger
Plains x23

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thought Scour.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Coati Scavenger.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 4
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
! Bot1.Target()
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Coati Scavenger; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 4
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
